  <main>

    <section class=3D"block" id=3D"summary">
      <h2>1. Executive summary</h2>
      <p class=3D"section-sub">Would a portfolio manager trust this for sto=
ck selection, valuation review, portfolio construction and an investment-co=
mmittee discussion?</p>

      <div class=3D"verdict">
        <span>=E2=9A=96=EF=B8=8F</span>
        <div>
          <b>Mostly yes =E2=80=94 with one methodology gap and one integrat=
ion gap that would come up in the first five minutes of committee review.</=
b>
          <p style=3D"margin:8px 0 0;font-size:14px">The valuation, technic=
al, portfolio and risk engines are individually sound =E2=80=94 every formu=
la traced back to real inputs, every disclosed heuristic actually disclosed=
, every edge case tested this session degraded gracefully rather than crash=
ing or fabricating a number. The two P0 findings are not calculation bugs; =
they're scope and integration gaps: the DCF engine runs on any company rega=
rdless of whether a discounted-cash-flow model is the right tool for that b=
usiness (it isn't, for banks), and the platform's two halves =E2=80=94 the =
original Buy/Hold/Sell rating and the new risk/valuation depth =E2=80=94 we=
re built in the same repository but never introduced to each other.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class=3D"two">
        <div class=3D"card">
          <h3 style=3D"margin:0 0 8px;font-size:14.5px">What holds up</h3>
          <ul class=3D"plain">
            <li>DCF math is internally consistent =E2=80=94 hand-verified a=
gainst NTPC's real WACC/growth inputs.</li>
            <li>Negative/unavailable-FCF handling never fabricates a fair v=
alue =E2=80=94 verified across 9 real companies.</li>
            <li>Correlation matrix is symmetric with a unit diagonal at 6 a=
nd 9 stocks.</li>
            <li>Weight normalization is exact under every tested condition,=
 including oversubscription.</li>
            <li>Single-stock and single-sector portfolios degrade gracefull=
y, no crashes.</li>
            <li>Cache-first startup performance fix from Phase 2 holds at l=
arger scale (verified at 10 stocks).</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class=3D"card">
          <h3 style=3D"margin:0 0 8px;font-size:14.5px">What needs Phase 3 =
before it scales</h3>
          <ul class=3D"plain">
            <li>DCF has no sector gate =E2=80=94 produces a misleading numb=
er for banks today.</li>
            <li>Rating tags don't reflect the new risk/DCF signals at all.<=
/li>
            <li>Sector-risk lookup misses an entire seeded watchlist (Defen=
ce).</li>
            <li>One seeded ticker (PGCIL.NS) has been silently broken since=
 it was seeded.</li>
            <li>Zero automated tests protect any of the new pure-math modul=
es.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class=3D"block" id=3D"gaps">
      <h2>2. Institutional gap analysis</h2>
      <p class=3D"section-sub">Ranked by what a professional reviewer would=
 flag first. P0 =3D fix before extending; P1 =3D fix soon; P2 =3D quality d=
ebt, no behavioral risk today.</p>

      <div class=3D"card finding">
        <span class=3D"sev critical">P0 =C2=B7 Valuation</span>
        <div>
          <h3>DCF has no sector gate =E2=80=94 produces a misleading fair v=
alue for banks</h3>
          <p>A levered free-cash-flow DCF is analytically invalid for a dep=
osit-taking/lending institution: "capital expenditure" and working capital =
don't correspond to a bank's balance sheet the way they do an operating com=
pany's. The model has no sector exclusion, so it runs anyway whenever Scree=
ner's generic Free Cash Flow line resolves as positive.</p>
          <div class=3D"evidence">Live query, HDFC Bank (Financial Services=
): <code>dcf.base =3D 2,280.46</code> vs <code>CMP =3D 725</code> =E2=80=94=
 an apparent ~3x "upside" that is a methodology mismatch, not a real signal=
. <code>dcf.wacc.waccPct =3D 12.71</code>, <code>reverseImpliedGrowthPct =
=3D -0.15</code>.</div>
          <p class=3D"fix"><b>Fix:</b> gate DCF/WACC/reverse-DCF/sensitivit=
y behind a Financial Services/Banking/Insurance/NBFC exclusion, with an exp=
licit "not meaningful for financial institutions" message =E2=80=94 same di=
sclosure pattern already used for EV/EBITDA.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class=3D"card finding">
        <span class=3D"sev critical">P0 =C2=B7 Scoring integration</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Rating tags have zero visibility into any Phase 2 signal</h3>
          <p>The Buy/Hold/Sell rating driving every tag across the Dashboar=
d, Top Opportunities and Opportunity status is still the original Phase 1 1=
2-factor model. It was never wired to the institutional risk composite, the=
 DCF read, or the new technical scorecard.</p>
          <div class=3D"evidence">Code-verified: <code>factors.mjs</code>'s=
 <code>technicalTrend()</code> still calls the Phase 1 <code>technicalTrend=
Signal()</code> from <code>yahooQuoteProvider.mjs</code>, not <code>technic=
alScorecard.mjs</code>. <code>scoringEngine.mjs</code> takes no <code>insti=
tutionalRisk</code> or <code>dcf</code> input at all.</div>
          <p class=3D"fix"><b>Fix (staged):</b> first, a visible "signal co=
nflict" flag wherever Rating disagrees materially with Risk/DCF (display-on=
ly, low risk). Folding these into <code>compositeScore</code> itself is a s=
coring-methodology change =E2=80=94 every Buy/Sell tag in the app would mov=
e =E2=80=94 and belongs in its own reviewed change, not bundled with the fl=
ag.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class=3D"card finding">
        <span class=3D"sev high">P1 =C2=B7 Risk framework</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Sector-risk lookup ignores <code style=3D"font-size:13px">ind=
ustry</code>, leaving whole watchlists undifferentiated</h3>
          <p>Screener classifies companies under both a broad <code style=
=3D"font-size:13px">sector</code> and a narrower <code style=3D"font-size:1=
3px">industry</code>. The sector-risk lookup only ever receives <code style=
=3D"font-size:13px">sector</code>.</p>
          <div class=3D"evidence">Live query: all 7 stocks in the seeded De=
fence watchlist are classified under the broad sector "Capital Goods" =E2=
=80=94 every one falls back to the generic default risk baseline (<code>mat=
ched: false</code>). The feature is silently non-functional for this entire=
 watchlist.</div>
          <p class=3D"fix"><b>Fix:</b> match against <code style=3D"font-si=
ze:13px">industry</code> first, falling back to <code style=3D"font-size:13=
px">sector</code>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class=3D"card finding">
        <span class=3D"sev high">P1 =C2=B7 Data integrity</span>
        <div>
          <h3>PGCIL.NS is not a valid Yahoo ticker</h3>
          <p>Power Grid trades as <code style=3D"font-size:13px">POWERGRID.=
NS</code>. An alias for <code style=3D"font-size:13px">PGCIL</code> exists =
for the Screener fundamentals fetch only =E2=80=94 not for the Yahoo quote =
fetch this row's price/technical data depends on.</p>
          <div class=3D"evidence">Live-confirmed: <code>fetchQuote('PGCIL.N=
S')</code> =E2=86=92 HTTP 404. This is the first row of the seeded Power wa=
tchlist. Pre-existing (not introduced this phase), never previously surface=
d.</div>
          <p class=3D"fix"><b>Fix:</b> reseed as <code style=3D"font-size:1=
3px">POWERGRID.NS</code>, or generalize the alias map to the Yahoo symbol t=
oo.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class=3D"card finding">
        <span class=3D"sev high">P1 =C2=B7 Resilience</span>
        <div>
          <h3>No retry or distinct failure state for a single failed fetch<=
/h3>
          <p>A correct, real ticker that transiently 404s renders identical=
ly to a nonexistent one =E2=80=94 a blank "unresolved" row with no indicati=
on of why.</p>
          <div class=3D"evidence">Live-confirmed: <code>LTIM.NS</code> (LTI=
Mindtree, a genuinely correct NSE ticker) 404'd on 3 consecutive attempts i=
n this environment.</div>
          <p class=3D"fix"><b>Fix:</b> one automatic retry with backoff wit=
hin a refresh pass; surface the failure reason distinctly from "never fetch=
ed."</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class=3D"card finding">
        <span class=3D"sev medium">P2 =C2=B7 Duplication</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Debt-trend calculation duplicated inside <span style=3D"font-=
family:var(--font-mono);font-size:14px">institutionalRisk.mjs</span></h3>
          <p><code style=3D"font-size:13px">financialRisk()</code> and <cod=
e style=3D"font-size:13px">governanceRisk()</code> each independently recom=
pute the identical 3-year borrowings-trend formula. Byte-identical today; e=
xactly the pattern that silently drifts the next time one copy gets tweaked=
.</p>
          <p class=3D"fix"><b>Fix:</b> compute once, pass into both.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class=3D"card finding">
        <span class=3D"sev medium">P2 =C2=B7 Duplication</span>
        <div>
          <h3>"Group stocks by sector" reimplemented three times</h3>
          <p><code style=3D"font-size:13px">portfolio.mjs</code>'s <code st=
yle=3D"font-size:13px">sectorAllocation()</code> and <code style=3D"font-si=
ze:13px">weightedSectorAllocation()</code>, plus <code style=3D"font-size:1=
3px">relativeValuation.mjs</code>'s peer grouping, each rebuild the same Ma=
p-by-sector logic independently.</p>
          <p class=3D"fix"><b>Fix:</b> one shared <code style=3D"font-size:=
13px">groupBySector()</code> helper.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class=3D"card finding">
        <span class=3D"sev medium">P2 =C2=B7 Dead code</span>
        <div>
          <h3><span style=3D"font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:14px">p=
earsonCorrelation()</span> export has no remaining callers</h3>
          <p>Superseded by <code style=3D"font-size:13px">correlationFromPr=
epared</code>/<code style=3D"font-size:13px">prepareSeries</code> when the =
correlation-matrix performance bug was fixed during Phase 2 implementation.=
 Grep-confirmed: zero call sites anywhere in the repository.</p>
          <p class=3D"fix"><b>Fix:</b> delete it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class=3D"card finding">
        <span class=3D"sev medium">P2 =C2=B7 Defensive coding</span>
        <div>
          <h3><span style=3D"font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:14px">c=
ard()</span> helper doesn't escape its own arguments</h3>
          <p>Every call site is individually responsible for pre-escaping d=
ynamic text. Hand-audited every Phase 2 call site by grep sweep: none curre=
ntly leak unescaped scraped/user content =E2=80=94 not an active vulnerabil=
ity =E2=80=94 but the safety depends on every future call site remembering =
the rule rather than the helper enforcing it.</p>
          <p class=3D"fix"><b>Fix:</b> escape by default, add an explicit o=
pt-out for the few legitimate raw-HTML cases like <code style=3D"font-size:=
13px">infoIcon()</code>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class=3D"card finding">
        <span class=3D"sev medium">P2 =C2=B7 Label consistency</span>
        <div>
          <h3><span style=3D"font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:14px">p=
ct()</span>'s forced "+" prefix misapplied to non-directional magnitudes</h=
3>
          <p>WACC, annualized volatility and position-weight % are inherent=
ly non-negative, yet render with a "+" that visually implies a directional =
figure =E2=80=94 e.g. "Largest position +16.67%," "WACC +8.73%." Confirmed =
across the Valuation and Portfolio deep-dive screenshots taken this session=
.</p>
          <p class=3D"fix"><b>Fix:</b> add a <code style=3D"font-size:13px"=
>pctAbs()</code> formatter for magnitude-only percentages; reserve <code st=
yle=3D"font-size:13px">pct()</code> for genuinely directional figures.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class=3D"card finding">
        <span class=3D"sev low">P3 =C2=B7 Disclosed limitation</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Bull/Bear DCF band width is fixed, not sector-calibrated</h3>
          <p>Clamped to [3pp, 15pp] regardless of a stock's actual historic=
al growth dispersion =E2=80=94 for genuinely cyclical names (commodities, c=
ement, sugar) this likely understates real earnings-cycle risk. Already lab=
eled Heuristic; restated here as a known limitation, not a defect.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class=3D"card finding">
        <span class=3D"sev low">P3 =C2=B7 Disclosed limitation</span>
        <div>
          <h3>No scoring formula in this app is empirically calibrated</h3>
          <p>Every risk/scoring coefficient across both phases (institution=
al risk, the 12-factor model, technical scores) is a reasonable-looking lin=
ear heuristic, not backtested against realized defaults, drawdowns or downg=
rades =E2=80=94 because this app has no historical-outcomes data source to =
calibrate against. Inherent to the whole scoring philosophy, already disclo=
sed via the Heuristic tier tag.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

